# Git Standards

## 1. Branch Model

Three permanent branch types exist across projects:

| Branch | Stability | Deployed to |
|---|---|---|
| `master` / `main` | Always stable — mirrors production code | PRE (3-branch model) / PRO (2-branch model) |
| `develop` | Integration — code not yet approved for production | PRE |
| `production` | Optional, high-change projects only | PRO |

**Absolute rules:**
- **Direct commits to `master`, `main`, or `develop` are forbidden.** All integrations must go through a Pull Request.
- `develop` originates from `master`/`main`.
- In 3-branch projects, deploying to PRO always requires a PR from `master` → `production`.

### CI/CD Environment Mapping

| Model | Branch | Environment |
|---|---|---|
| 3-branch | `production` | PRO |
| 3-branch | `master` / `main` | PRE |
| 3-branch | `develop` | PRE |
| 2-branch | `master` / `main` | PRO |
| 2-branch | `develop` | PRE |

---

## 2. Branch Types

Each working branch corresponds to **exactly one User Story**.

### Feature

A feature branch implements an evolutionary development aligned with a User Story.

- **Created from**: `develop`
- **Merged into**: `develop` (via Pull Request)
- **Naming pattern**: `feature/YYYYMMDD_[ticketID_if_exists]_description_without_spaces`
- **Examples**: `feature/20260514_18799_new_position_search`, `feature/20260514_candidate_profile`
- **After merge**: branch must be deleted from remote.

### Hotfix

A hotfix branch implements a corrective or urgent fix aligned with a User Story.

- **Created from**: `master` or `main`
- **Merged into**: **both** `master`/`main` AND `develop` (two separate Pull Requests)
- **Naming pattern**: `hotfix/YYYYMMDD_[ticketID_if_exists]_description_without_spaces`
- **Examples**: `hotfix/20260514_18800_fix_login_token`, `hotfix/20260514_payment_null_pointer`
- **After merge**: branch must be deleted from remote.

---

## 3. Commit and Push Rules

- **Push immediately after every commit.** Never accumulate local commits — local and remote branches must remain in sync at all times.
- All commit messages must be written in **English**.
- Commits must be atomic and focused on a single logical change.
- Never commit directly to `master`, `main`, or `develop`.

---

## 4. Pull Request Rules

### Before opening a PR

1. Merge the base branch into the working branch locally and resolve any conflicts:
   - For **features**: `git merge develop` into the feature branch.
   - For **hotfixes**: `git merge master` (or `main`) into the hotfix branch.
2. Verify the build and tests pass on the merged result before opening the PR.

### PR targets

| Branch type | PR target |
|---|---|
| `feature/*` | `develop` |
| `hotfix/*` | `master` / `main` **and** `develop` (two separate PRs) |

### Reviewer requirements

| Target branch | Minimum approvals |
|---|---|
| `develop` | 1 reviewer |
| `master` / `main` / `production` | 2 reviewers |

### After the PR is merged

- Delete the working branch from remote immediately.

---

## 5. Tags and Versioning

Tags are only created when **explicitly requested** — not on every release.

- **Format**: `X.Y.Z_snake_case_description`
  - `X`: Major version
  - `Y`: Minor version
  - `Z`: Hotfix version
- **Examples**: `1.2.2_new_collection_standards`, `2.0.0_dln_json_integration`
- Follows [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/).

---

## 6. AI Agent Git Checklist

Verify all applicable items before each Git operation:

### Before creating a branch
- [ ] Branch type matches the User Story type (`feature` for evolutionary, `hotfix` for corrective/urgent).
- [ ] Branch is created from the correct base: `develop` for features, `master`/`main` for hotfixes.
- [ ] Branch name follows `type/YYYYMMDD_[ticketID_]description` with underscores and no spaces.

### Before each commit
- [ ] Commit message is in English.
- [ ] Changes are atomic and focused.
- [ ] Push to remote immediately after committing.

### Before opening a Pull Request
- [ ] Base branch has been merged into the working branch locally.
- [ ] Conflicts resolved and build/tests pass.
- [ ] PR targets the correct branch: `develop` for features; `master`/`main` for hotfixes (plus a second PR to `develop` for hotfixes).
- [ ] Required reviewer count noted: 1 for `develop`, 2 for `master`/`main`/`production`.

### After Pull Request is merged
- [ ] Working branch deleted from remote.
- [ ] For hotfixes: confirm **both** PRs (to `master` and to `develop`) are merged before deleting the branch.
